- op: discuss  # 9d92
  at: '2026-06-19T11:02:16Z'  # 9d92
  by: agent  # 9d92
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9d92
  clock: 7  # 9d92
  nonce: 9d92  # 9d92
  message: "PART 1 of emission-parity F2 merged: PR #4228 (origin/dev 8f11136fb9). CJS module bindings now reach call-graph parity with ESM, and .mjs/.cjs/.mts/.cts are discovered. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-probe of the analyzer on a crafted CJS file): `const fs=require('fs'); const {exec}=require('child_process'); function r(){return fs.readFileSync('x');} function e(){return exec('ls');}` now emits 2 unresolved 'calls' edges (r->fs:readFileSync, e->child_process:exec) where it previously emitted ZERO calls (only the 2 import edges) — restoring io-boundary visibility for CommonJS Node code (the fs.writeFileSync/child_process.exec/http.get harm in the item statement). .cjs files now analyzed (were undiscovered); .mts/.cts tagged typescript. Mechanism: _extract_namespace_imports/_extract_named_imports now harvest require default+destructured bindings, routing through the existing WI-vurop (namespace) and WI-banaf (named) unresolved-call paths; aliased destructures key on canonical export name. 11 new tests in test_js_ts.py, js_ts.py 100% cov. STATUS STAYS todo_hard — NOT closed. Remaining for F2 closure (separate larger-blast-radius slices): (a) service-worker idiom still emits only the file node + 0 edges (top-level anonymous-callback bodies: caches.open()/fetch()/cache.put() — receivers not in JS_KNOWN_GLOBALS, callbacks not extracted as function nodes); (b) anonymous-callback function-NODE extraction (shifts corpus symbol counts); (c) bare global I/O calls like fetch()."  # 9d92
- op: discuss  # 70ab
  at: '2026-06-19T14:40:57Z'  # 70ab
  by: agent  # 70ab
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 70ab
  clock: 8  # 70ab
  nonce: 70ab  # 70ab
  message: "PART 2 of emission-parity F2 merged: PR #4230 (origin/dev da95f235e0). Browser/worker global I/O calls now reach the io-boundary catalog. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (analyzer re-probe): the service-worker idiom (a file built ENTIRELY from top-level 'self.addEventListener(\"fetch\", e => caches.open(...))' callbacks) now emits 2 unresolved I/O 'calls' edges (caches:open, attributed to the file pseudo-node) where it previously emitted 1 symbol (file) + ZERO edges — directly fixing the WI-zavad frozen-substrate reproduction (service-worker.js full of caches.open()/fetch() that reported zero I/O). Mechanism: caches/indexedDB joined JS_KNOWN_GLOBALS (member-call Case 3b); new JS_KNOWN_GLOBAL_CALLS={fetch} gives bare fetch() an unresolved-call path keyed on the catalog's 'module: fetch, functions:[fetch]' shape (intra-repo/imported fetch resolution still wins — guarded by a test). Catalog (io_primitives/javascript.yaml) already listed caches/indexedDB/fetch; the gap was purely analyzer emission. 5 new tests, js_ts.py 100% cov, 19140 passed. STATUS STAYS todo_hard. The io-boundary INVISIBILITY harm (the P0's central claim) is now addressed across all three surfaces: Node CJS (Part 1, PR #4228), Node ESM (pre-existing), browser/Service-Worker (Part 2, PR #4230). REMAINING for full F2/WI-zavad closure (one deferred slice, separate bakeoff-validated PR — HIGH BLAST RADIUS): anonymous-callback function-NODE extraction (the WS-linker file-anchor facet F159.A2-c) — _extract_symbols still doesn't extract general top-level addEventListener callbacks as symbols, so they produce no function nodes (only the file node); fixing it adds anonymous symbols corpus-wide and shifts symbol/centrality/dead-code counts, so it needs awaits_bakeoff_validation. OPS NOTE: PR #4229 (Part-2 first cut) was closed after auto-pr's rebase mangled its base onto pre-slice-1 21532da5dc (diverged, non-FF, re-applied dev's slice-1 changes) — Forgejo's mergeability check stuck at 'checking' => persistent HTTP 405. A clean FF-able re-cut (#4230) merged immediately. Lesson: a 'checking' 405 can be a non-FF branch, not a remote outage — verify parent==origin/dev tip first."  # 70ab
